ated event not just seven random  people who were picked to fight each  other the owner of this tournament is a  man by the name of zhang and he states  in the beginning of the tournament that  it will be very tough as everyone  attending are some of the greatest  fighters around the world this game even  recommends that you upgrade your health  more so that the dlc is easier but i  decided against it our first match is  between a bunch of random martial  artists this is very similar to the  martial art clubs  in the main game except with hazards  we're then instructed to follow the path  to the back of the island where we get  to see some more fights with other  contestants until our first actual fight  arrives  unlike the typical no-name contestants  all the bosses have unique fighting  styles and moves making it harder to  block them which i liked a lot  most of the moves enemies throw in the  game are telegraphed quite easily but i  found myself getting hit by these more  making it seem like an actual back and  forth fight not just a one-sided brawl  the bosses also have quick time events  like the grapplers do and yes while  after some time they do get a little  repetitive and telegraphed the first few  times did mix me up  because i didn't know a button to press  when a grappler grabs you from behind  you would know immediately to spam y  to break out of it it's not a challenge  anymore but by changing the button  slightly for the bosses it makes it a  bit more refreshing  after the fight we continue to explore  the island until we meet a contestant  who offers us tea which we find out has  been poisoned  it seems like the rich people who  attended the fight wanted to see someone  get poisoned and fight someone and that  just happened to be us  we then beat george who has a lot of  ground moves more than we've seen all  game he's pretty much a pushover though  if you remember the button inputs as i  don't think he landed a single grapple  the entire fight i'm 